\details{
These zero-handling and processing-ledger conventions apply to the curated
GlycoPOST datasets. CPTAC loaders retain source log2 values in metadata and
use \code{2^source_value} in the assay; source zeros become 1. See
\link{glyhub_CPTAC_CCRCC} and \code{\link[=glyhub_catalog]{glyhub_catalog()}}. Locally staged non-CPTAC
datasets retain source numeric values and zeros without added normalization,
imputation or inverse transformation. Prefer original intensities where
available; processed-only matrices explicitly document their source scale.
\code{raw_abundance} means the source numeric matrix, not a guarantee that authors
supplied unprocessed intensities. See each dataset's help and metadata.
The PXD019914 relative-ratio objects are a study-specific exception: assays
contain 2^x of author-normalized log2 ratios, with the original log2 matrix
retained. These are linear relative ratios, not reconstructed raw intensity.

Source-only literature resources use \code{glyhub_load(id, kind = "raw")} to return
a verified file path. Here raw means original source asset, not instrument-raw
intensity. Signed author-processed values are retained without transformation;
some entries have no curated SE object; source-only IDs have no same-named
loader function. PXD019914 also provides separately named relative-ratio SEs.
See \link{glyhub_literature_sources} for scales, sample mapping and provenance.

Zero-valued abundances are represented as \code{NA} in the distributed abundance
assay. This representation differs from the original source tables, which
remain available in metadata. Missing values are not imputed, and abundances
are not renormalized after this conversion. Zero-valued times and categorical
annotations are unchanged.

For GPST000738, measurements with unresolved source-table conflicts are also
\code{NA}. \code{metadata(x)$processing_masks} distinguishes original missing entries,
source not-detected entries, conflicts and zero conversions. Masks may overlap.
For GPST000643, not-detected retention-time entries are recorded separately
from zero-valued quantitative measurements.

\code{metadata(x)$raw_abundance} preserves the original numerical matrix.
\code{raw_text}, source tables and \code{processing_ledger} retain source notation,
cell coordinates and the explanation for each processed value. Original AUCs
and retention times are available for GPST000643. These provenance matrices
are not additional abundance assays and may use different units.

\code{rowData(x)} retains source feature labels, typed glyrepr compositions and
structures where supported. A \code{glycan_structure} column is present only when
at least one feature has a valid structural annotation; unannotated features
in that column remain \code{NA}. If none has a structural annotation, the column
is absent. Putative assignments remain putative; ambiguous
linkages are not completed. Unconverted notation and annotation disagreements
are retained explicitly. Source mass/isomer labels are not universal IDs.
Consult individual feature annotations when an experiment includes more than
one glycan class.

\code{colData(x)} contains source conditions and observation labels. Common numeric
and logical source types are preserved when combining panels, with typed
missing values for absent or conflicting observations. Genuinely mixed source
types retain their original text rather than being guessed or coerced to numbers.
A source label
such as Sample 1 or Replicate 1 does not by itself establish biological
replication, independence or pairing across tables. Each object's \code{source},
\code{doi} and \code{license} metadata identify its references and source-data license.
Source-data licenses are separate from the package code license.
